- tinytest-console-error (tests/tinytest.js:53): under qjsm console.error is
  undefined, so a failing test throws "not a function" out of run() instead of
  printing the failure, and the summary line never appears (found while
  debugging a failing assertion in tests/test-pointer-helpers.js).

    import { tests, eq } from './tinytest.js';
    await tests({ 'fails'() { eq(1, 2); } });


- example-zlib-missing-os-import (examples/zlib.js:11): the example uses
  os.open() but only imports from std, so it dies with "'os' is not defined"
  right after printing the z_stream (found while testing the regenerated
  lib/zlib.js; identical with the original files).

    qjsm examples/zlib.js

- zlib-z_stream-from-undefined-class (lib/zlib-extras.js:168): z_stream.from()
  sets the prototype to z_stream_s.prototype, but no z_stream_s exists (the
  class is called z_stream), so it throws a ReferenceError.

    import { z_stream } from './lib/zlib-extras.js'; z_stream.from(0);

- zlib-deflateinit-default-level (lib/zlib-extras.js:181): deflateInit() defaults
  its level to Z_DEFAULT_STRATEGY (0, which is Z_NO_COMPRESSION) instead of
  Z_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION (-1), so calling it with no level stores uncompressed
  data (carried over unchanged from the old lib/zlib.js).

    import { z_stream, deflateInit } from './lib/zlib-extras.js'; deflateInit(new z_stream());

- inspect-short-bigint-unhandled (../qjs-modules/quickjs-inspect.c:1423):
  console.log of a BigInt small enough to be a QuickJS short bigint (tag 7,
  JS_TAG_SHORT_BIG_INT) throws "Unhandled value tag in inspect_value: 7";
  a large BigInt (2n**70n) prints fine. found printing ptr() results.

    console.log(5n);

- tinytest-eq-no-deep-compare (tests/tinytest.js:73): eq/assertEquals
  compares with loose inequality, so two equal arrays or objects always
  fail, and the message prints both as the same string (for example
  "a,b" != "a,b"), which hides the cause (found writing
  tests/test-gen-bindings-cxx.js).

    import { tests, eq } from './tinytest.js';
    await tests({ 'equal arrays'() { eq(['a', 'b'], ['a', 'b']); } });

- buffer-arg-dataview-segfault (js-helpers.c:51): js_buf() resolves an
  ArrayBuffer or TypedArray but not a DataView, so a DataView passed as a
  "buffer"/"pointer" argument silently becomes address 0 and the callee gets
  NULL (strlen crashes); ptr(new DataView(buf)) returns null. found probing
  bun:ffi parity.

    import { dlopen, ptr } from 'ffi';
    const { symbols } = dlopen('libc.so.6', { strlen: { args: ['buffer'], returns: 'u64' } });
    symbols.strlen(new DataView(new Uint8Array([104, 105, 0]).buffer));

- test-js-free-of-string (test.js:134): strdup is defined with a char * return, which the legacy API gives as a js string, and that string is then passed to free(), which aborts with invalid pointer (same before legacy.js). found porting the legacy clients.

    qjsm test.js

- to-array-buffer-no-pointer (ffi.c:330): toArrayBuffer() and toBuffer() called with no pointer, undefined or an object return an empty ArrayBuffer instead of throwing (the legacy-form fallback treats the argument as address 0); bun throws. found comparing the api with bun.

    import { toArrayBuffer } from 'ffi';
    console.log(toArrayBuffer().byteLength);
